          ],
          "content": "Chapter 6 — Pressure, Winds, Storms, and Cyclones"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.892,
            0.029,
            0.917,
            0.045
          ],
          "content": "95"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.082,
            0.744,
            0.139
          ],
          "content": "(iii) A water tank is placed on the roof of a building at a height ‘H’. To get water with more pressure on the ground floor, one has to"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.14,
            0.719,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": "(a) increase the height $\\mathrm { ^ { \\circ } H ^ { \\prime } }$ at which the tank is placed."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.161,
            0.723,
            0.182
          ],
          "content": "(b) decrease the height ‘H’ at which the tank is placed."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.182,
            0.744,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": "(c) replace the tank with another tank of the same height that can hold more water."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.221,
            0.744,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "(d) replace the tank with another tank of the same height that can hold less water."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.261,
            0.649,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": "(iv) Two vessels, A and B contain water up to the same level as shown in Fig. 6.22. $\\mathrm { P _ { A } }$ and $\\mathrm { P _ { \\mathrm { { } _ { B } } } }$ is the pressure at the bottom of the vessels. $\\mathrm { F _ { A } }$ and $\\mathrm { F _ { \\mathrm { { \\scriptsize ~ B } } } }$ is the force exerted by the water at the bottom of the vessels A and B."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.356,
            0.37,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{A}}=\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{B}}, \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{A}}=\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{B}}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.672,
            0.266,
            0.876,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.377,
            0.369,
            0.399
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{A}}=\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{B}}, \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{A}}<\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{B}}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.398,
            0.37,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{A}}<\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{B}}, \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{A}}=\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{B}}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.419,
            0.37,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": "(d) $\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{A}}>\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{B}}, \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{A}}>\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{B}}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.439,
            0.744,
            0.477
          ],
          "content": "2. State whether the following statements are True [T] or False [F]."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.477,
            0.744,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": "(i) Air flows from a region of higher pressure to a region of lower pressure. [ ]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.517,
            0.645,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Liquids exert pressure only at the bottom of a container. [ ]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.556,
            0.644,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Weather is stormy at the eye of a cyclone. [ ]"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.667,
            0.503,
            0.86,
            0.605
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
